Author: “zhangchenxu” <zhangchenxu.2025@bytedance.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 20:53:17 2026 +0800

    Fix the stage 2 audit's findings (AUD16-001 to 008) and the dictation pause
    
    A family table that cannot be read is no longer a first boot: adults count as
    having a PIN, nothing overwrites it, each PIN entry tries the read again.
    A recording belongs to its member; a closed space ends the AI's turn; events
    that say whose they are go only while that member is here. A paused stream
    stops at the pause. Resources are checked again after the restart and a failed
    write keeps them to do. A factory reset now only marks and restarts: the next
    boot wipes before any service runs, a power cut repeats it, and the card's part
    waits for a card. The dictation pause counts quiet frames: subtracting two
    tasks' clocks could wrap (CI). hal_net_sim no longer reads a message it gave away.
    
    Tests and negative controls: design §15.3.1. The audit run was cut off by the
    provider's classifier; its partial report is kept.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

