commit 42f1f2205b5228fdb9a1ad6975fe73348e9b765e
Author: “zhangchenxu” <zhangchenxu.2025@bytedance.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 4 18:39:44 2026 +0800

    system: what the audit of the first stage found
    
    The Codex audit (docs/audits/2026-11-04-codex-services, round 14) found five high and six medium, none critical:
    
    - A file that is there and cannot be read now was taken for no file: the collection opened empty and writes on top of
      it were reported durable and lost on the next load. It does not open now, and says so (AUD15-001).
    - Deleting /family took the members' private folders with it. The places everyone sees cannot be deleted or moved;
      removing a member clears their folder directly (AUD15-002).
    - A page of Chinese cut before a whole character said it was the end of the file (AUD15-003).
    - Records over 2 KB came back to the AI cut, as invalid JSON and a success (AUD15-004).
    - A notification for one member could end up in the inbox of another who came in between, and be told to their AI
      (AUD15-005).
    - Two tasks changing the interruptions at once could leave it ringing: one task at a time applies what the table says
      now, the others say there is more to do (AUD15-006).
    - What a person said yes to ran for whoever was using the device by the time it started: a call can be bound to a
      member (AUD15-007).
    - A zone change was not kept for the alarms, so the next boot rang at the old zone's time. It is saved, and worked out
      again at boot for what a power cut kept from being saved (AUD15-008).
    - The AI surface test did not notice a capability losing its schema, though the design said it would: it now parses the
      tool list the hub gets, against a table of what each must be given (AUD15-009).
    - An app whose state could not be handed to the flash was stopped as if saved. It stays, and closing says so
      (AUD15-010).
    - Locked and kept awake by something in the background, the battery was not looked at (AUD15-011).
    
    Each with a test; tests/integration/races.c arranges the three races with semaphores, as the audit's probes did.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

